<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    The app's entitlements. Deliberately EMPTY.

    This build signs with a free personal team, which can grant none of the four this app once
    asked for. An entitlement a team cannot grant is a signing failure rather than a runtime one,
    so they are absent instead of requested. Config.xcconfig lists each one and what its absence
    costs; the short version is push, Universal Links, joining a Wi-Fi network and reading the
    SSID back. None of them is needed to record a session.

    This file replaced a pair — iosApp.entitlements asking for all four, and
    iosApp-personal.entitlements holding an empty dict — selected by a gitignored override. With
    one team there is one answer, so there is one file.

    Live Activities need nothing here. The check-in widget is started and updated by the app
    itself (MonadPresenceBridge), not pushed to, so it works on this signing path.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
